Historical 0.9 native-tool and480KiB extension
The 0.9 build contracts introduced 491520-byte output, keeping the source/token
buffers and4MiB hosted arena unchanged. Parser state moves32768 bytes beyond
the historical448KiB layout;0.10 later enlarges decoded-template storage. The real-mode output remains
limited to16KiB. biosmove supplies bounded INT15/AH87 transfers to the Zero
BIOS loader; loading policy stays in bios.zero. Native app targets provide
Zero-owned memory input/output and exit services, enabling Zero and Ezero
execution inside the guest. The1MiB bundle and8MiB workspace are loaded by
BIOS or allocated by UEFI before entering the kernel. Capacity and full-copy
evidence: verification/guest-bundle-480k/. Native compiler execution evidence:
